#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
apply_expiry_card.py — EXPIRY_CARD_20260929

Week + month P/L card sent to Telegram at 15:40 on every weekly-expiry day
(NIFTY Tuesday, or the Monday before a Tuesday holiday), right after the
daily card. Backend only. Run from the repo root:

    python3 apply_expiry_card.py --check        # verify prerequisites, no writes
    python3 apply_expiry_card.py                # apply
    python3 apply_expiry_card.py --allow-dirty  # if git shows the targets modified on purpose

RUN ONLY THIS SCRIPT — it carries every payload (VET_PANEL_V2 scar); a
pre-placed file trips the mixed-state guard.

What changes
  NEW  backend/app/api/telegram_expiry_card.py   renderer + ExpiryCardData + fixtures
                                                 (Midnight palette shared with the daily card)
  NEW  backend/app/api/telegram_expiry_data.py   week / month buckets from the dashboard's
                                                 legs read (fleet_today_routes._legs_for,
                                                 _week_from / _month_from, _positions / _baskets),
                                                 session cells + expected-expiry cells
  NEW  backend/app/api/telegram_expiry_send.py   is_expiry_day (live_dte == 0), caption,
                                                 sendPhoto + text fallback
  NEW  backend/app/tests/preview_expiry_card.py  --fixture empty|live|fleet or the real DB
  NEW  backend/app/tests/test_expiry_card.py     76-check suite (acceptance gate, rolls back)
  EDIT backend/app/services/telegram_scheduler.py  ANCHORED: import, _last_expiry_date,
                                                 _tick calls _handle_expiry_summary after the
                                                 daily card, + _handle/_dispatch/run_now methods
  EDIT backend/app/api/telegram_api.py           ANCHORED: GET /debug/run-expiry-summary
  desktop/src-tauri/backend/...                  mirrored when present

Prerequisites (asserted)
  * EOD_CARD_V2_20260929 applied (palette / layout tokens are imported from it)
  * FLEET_KPIS_PERIOD_20260928 in fleet_today_routes.py (_week_from / _month_from)
  * DTE_LOT_MULT_LIVE_20260911 (app/engine/dte_live.py — live_dte)
  * anchors unique in telegram_scheduler.py and telegram_api.py; fence absent

Rebuild afterwards:  ./desktop/build-scalp.sh backend
Preview any time:    cd backend && python3 app/tests/preview_expiry_card.py [--fixture fleet]
Send now:            GET /debug/run-expiry-summary   (works on non-expiry days too; subtitle says so)
"""

